{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","permalink_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/FFmpeg:4b0fad0...FFmpeg:55bf0e6","diff_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"4b0fad0c61a9ba93e7bc8a469dac8ff208a45d7b","node_id":"C_kwDOABiiStoAKDRiMGZhZDBjNjFhOWJhOTNlN2JjOGE0NjlkYWM4ZmYyMDhhNDVkN2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Baptiste Coudurier","email":"baptiste.coudurier@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T21:40:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"Baptiste Coudurier","email":"baptiste.coudurier@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T22:28:14Z"},"message":"avcodec/svq1dec: set the key flag on intra frames\n\nIntra frames are self-contained and were only marked as\nAV_PICTURE_TYPE_I, so every decoded SVQ1 frame had key_frame=0 and\nplayers waiting for a keyframe never showed the video.\n\nFixes #25938.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Baptiste Coudurier <baptiste.coudurier@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"257b6f81fc8886f5cab0425505aa3c88573f9326","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/trees/257b6f81fc8886f5cab0425505aa3c88573f9326"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/commits/4b0fad0c61a9ba93e7bc8a469dac8ff208a45d7b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/4b0fad0c61a9ba93e7bc8a469dac8ff208a45d7b","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/4b0fad0c61a9ba93e7bc8a469dac8ff208a45d7b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/4b0fad0c61a9ba93e7bc8a469dac8ff208a45d7b/comments","author":{"login":"bcoudurier","id":918644,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxODY0NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/918644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier","html_url":"https://github.com/bcoudurier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"bcoudurier","id":918644,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxODY0NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/918644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier","html_url":"https://github.com/bcoudurier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcoudurier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a948f8e34a21ab457d533fe7ad18ec89fe9d5d07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/a948f8e34a21ab457d533fe7ad18ec89fe9d5d07","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/a948f8e34a21ab457d533fe7ad18ec89fe9d5d07"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","node_id":"C_kwDOABiiStoAKDU1YmYwZTZjZDVhNDZiMjZiMGViZDIzNzRhZDI2MjVhNzEzM2U0ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nicholas Carlini","email":"nicholas@carlini.com","date":"2026-03-14T15:39:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"michaelni","email":"michael@niedermayer.cc","date":"2026-03-14T21:01:41Z"},"message":"avformat/mpegts: remove JPEG-XS early return on invalid header_size\n\nnew_pes_packet() moves a buffer with pkt->buf = pes->buffer before\nJPEG-XS validation. If header_size > pkt->size, an early return leaves\npes->buffer as a stale alias of pkt->buf with refcount 1. Later,\nmpegts_read_packet() calls av_packet_unref(), freeing the buffer\nthrough pkt->buf. The flush loop then re-enters new_pes_packet() and\ndereferences the dangling pes->buffer; a second path hits it via\nav_buffer_unref() in handle_packets() after a seek.\n\nDrop the early return. The packet is delivered with AV_PKT_FLAG_CORRUPT\nset, matching the PES-size-mismatch case above, and the function falls\nthrough to the normal cleanup path. The else guards the header trim so\npkt->data/pkt->size stay valid for the memset.\n\nFixes: use after free\nFixes regression since 16f89d342e.\n\nFound-by: Nicholas Carlini <nicholas@carlini.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ff5166a6f35858f8e497fc2badda2dac1f2c8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/trees/9ff5166a6f35858f8e497fc2badda2dac1f2c8a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/commits/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/55bf0e